One common algorithm for sorting an array of integers is the QuickSort algorithm. Here is a basic implementation in Python:

```
def quicksort(arr):
    if len(arr) <= 1:
        return arr
    else:
        pivot = arr[0]
        left = [x for x in arr[1:] if x < pivot]
        middle = [x for x in arr[1:] if x == pivot]
        right = [x for x in arr[1:] if x > pivot]
        return quicksort(left) + middle + quicksort(right)
```

