Cassini is a technology that allows Visual Studio to host websites as standalone applications without requiring IIS. It was included in VS2005 and VS2008. Each ASP.NET web application you start in Visual Studio results in a separate Cassini process. 

If you want to stop these Cassini processes, you have a couple of options:

1. Kill them manually: This is the most straightforward method. You can do it from the command line or from Task Manager.

2. Configure Visual Studio to use IIS: You can tell Visual Studio to use IIS instead of Cassini. This can be done in the project properties for ASP.NET applications.

